	(text "Test Points -- bring-up probing"
		(at 25.40 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "99999999-0000-4000-8000-000000000001")
	)
	(text "Wired: each pad sits on a global label (no drawn wires), same convention\nas power_bms. TP1 +3V3, TP2 VBAT, TP3/TP4 GND, TP5 FW_MARKER = U4 pin 8\n(P0.22) on radio_mcu.kicad_sch.\n\nDeliberately minimal. The tag is one module plus a battery chain, and the\nDWM3001C's internals are not reachable -- its UWB transceiver, MCU and both\nantennas are inside the package, so there is nothing useful to probe there.\nSWD already comes out on J3 (programming_debug.kicad_sch), so debug access\nis covered without a test point.\n\nWhat is worth probing:\n\n  POWER -- TP1 and TP2 are the two rails that matter. TP2 (VBAT) also lets\n  the battery chain be checked independently of the regulator, which is the\n  natural first question when a worn device will not start.\n\n  GROUND -- two, so a scope and a meter can be attached at once without\n  sharing a return.\n\n  TIMING MARKER -- TP5 on a spare nRF52833 GPIO. Firmware can toggle it\n  around a ranging exchange, which turns tag-side timing into something a\n  scope can see. On a system budgeted in nanoseconds that is worth one pad.\n\nThere is no power switch on this board (resolved 2026-09-19), so the tag is\nlive whenever a battery is connected -- TP1/TP2 are the only way to confirm\nrail state without disconnecting the cell."
		(at 25.40 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "99999999-0000-4000-8000-000000000002")
	)
